      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 748,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both てある and ておく express actions done for future purposes, but with key differences. てある focuses on the resulting state after the action is performed, e.g. 窓が開けてある ('The window has been opened.', when it remains open for some purpose). In contrast, ておく emphasizes the action itself, focusing on preparation, e.g. 窓を開けておいた ('I opened the window.', implying that it was for future benefit.). Note also the different particles used.",
